# ScanPro Backend AI Rules & Guidelines

- Follow Modular Layered Architecture: `src/modules/<name>/(controller|dto|repository|routes|service|validation)`.
- Use TypeScript with strict types. Run `npx tsc --noEmit` to verify type checks.
- All requests MUST be validated with Zod schemas in `*.validation.ts`.
- Protected routes MUST use `authenticate` middleware.
- Database queries MUST use Prisma Client with transactions for multi-record operations.
- Mandatory Prisma Migrations: Whenever `prisma/schema.prisma` changes and needs a DB update, ALWAYS create a migration in `prisma/migrations/` (plus `npx prisma generate && npx prisma validate`) so production `npx prisma migrate deploy` succeeds cleanly; never skip migrations or rely on `prisma db push`.
- Always return standard response JSON: `{ success: boolean, message?: string, data?: any, error?: any }`.
- NEVER rewrite or refactor unrelated working endpoints or architecture.
